  "body": "## What changed\n\n`camcraft-ui <file>` opens one file at start:\n\n- A model file (`.stl`, `.obj`, `.step`, `.stp`, and a Solidcraft `.sc` on native builds) is imported through `CommandKind::ImportFile`.\n- A project file (`.camproj`) is opened through `CommandKind::OpenProjectFile`.\n\nThese are the commands of the Model and Project dialogs and of a drop. The worker, the update-or-spawn decision and the refusals stay shared (`crates/ui/src/launch_file.rs`).\n\nThe file arguments come from the same walk over the arguments as the option check (`cli_options::files`). An option's value (`--gpu nvidia`) is never read as a file. More than one file, an unknown extension, or a path that is not a file is refused by name on the status line (`open refused: ...`). The app then starts with an empty project. `--help` shows `Usage: camcraft-ui [options] [file]` and a `File:` section.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/2462-open-file-argument.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Live app, debug build, macOS: `camcraft-ui --mcp-port 7915 testdata/models/solidcraft_for_beginners.sc`. MCP `get_job` returns the model `solidcraft_for_beginners`, 279602 facets, bounds (-62.5, -62.5, 0) to (62.5, 62.5, 85), `can_undo: true`. The `.sc` import takes about 100 s in a debug build.\n- Live app with `testdata/models/cube.stl`: `get_job` returns `cube`, 12 facets, bounds (0, 0, 0) to (1, 1, 1).\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/ui/src/launch_file_tests.rs`)\n\n- `the_files_are_the_arguments_that_are_no_option_and_no_value`\n- `help_shows_the_file_argument`\n- `no_file_queues_nothing`\n- `each_model_kind_is_imported_through_the_import_command` (STL, OBJ, STEP)\n- `a_solidcraft_design_is_imported`\n- `a_project_is_opened_through_the_open_command`\n- `a_file_that_cannot_be_opened_is_refused_by_name`\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick`: 9 steps, 0 failed (ui lib suite: 1095 passed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and Linux: not run. The change has no platform code.\n- macOS `open -a CamCraft part.sc`: macOS sends the file as an Apple Event, not as an argument. This change does not read Apple Events. To start the binary in the bundle with the path works.\n- A running window that takes a file from a second start (single instance): out of scope (#2462).\n\n## Why\n\nSolidcraft proposes a \"Send to CamCraft\" command (tangency-labs/solidcraft#18936, Solidcraft RFC 0001 phase 1) that starts CamCraft with a design's path. The linked-model follow-up is #2463.\n\nChangelog: `camcraft-ui <file>` opens a model or project file given on the command line (#2462).\nEffort: medium\nFork synced at v0.23.0 (branch from upstream main 1d3d93541).\n\nFixes #2462\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01MLU9aif5zm7mure23AKftd\n",
